{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And you shall take the anointing oil and pour it upon his head.</b> Rabbi Abraham ibn Ezra said (on Exodus 29:7) that this was before placing the turban upon his head, for upon his very head he pours the oil. And this is not correct in my eyes, for in the account of the matter it says, \"And he placed the turban upon his head\" etc. (Leviticus 8:9), and afterwards it says, \"And he took the anointing oil and anointed the Tabernacle\" etc. (Exodus 29:10 — in the execution narrative at Leviticus 8:10), and afterwards, \"And he poured of the anointing oil upon Aaron's head\" (Leviticus 8:12). But the correct interpretation is that the turban was wrapped all around and the middle of the head was exposed, and upon it he poured the oil. And if the anointing was over the entire head, according to Rashi's words, the pouring was at the place of laying tefillin, which he would leave exposed, and from there he would draw it in the shape of a Greek kappa."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "Ramban cites Ibn Ezra's comment as being on Exodus 29:7, but the biblical verses he quotes in the execution narrative (Leviticus 8:9, 8:10, 8:12) are referenced with mixed addresses — he gives Exodus 29:10 and 29:12 where the actual execution narrative is in Leviticus 8. These are rendered as Ramban wrote them."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:19:00.277122887Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}